  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Guaranteed Distributions\" is the term the whole Policy turns on, and it is built from nested clauses with carve-outs for amounts unavailable because of the Net Rate Cap, prepayment-related reductions and withholding or other governmental charges. What falls inside the guaranteed amount, and what is excluded as a Net Rate Cap or prepayment shortfall, is precisely the sort of coverage boundary parties litigate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.55},
     {"issue": "The definition makes coverage turn on amendments or modifications of the Pooling and Servicing Agreement and on Financial Security's consent, which is hard to square with the Policy's statement that it \"shall not be modified, altered or affected by any other agreement or instrument\" (c007). The two provisions treat the transaction documents' effect on the Policy differently.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Term of this Policy\" fixes both the commencement and the terminal date of coverage, and as drafted the end point is tied to a condition rather than a fixed date. Because the preference guarantee (c002) covers only distributions \"made during the Term\", the boundary of that period carries real consequence and is not self-evident.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.08},
     {"issue": "The Policy's insuring clause runs \"to each Trustee for the benefit of each Holder\" (c001) and defines Trustee as U.S. Bank (c015), yet the endorsement gives the notice, assignment and further-assurance functions to Wells Fargo as Trust Administrator (c019, c020). Which entity holds and may enforce the Policy rights is not squarely resolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": "The Trustee is the named beneficiary of the guarantee (c001) but the operative claim and assignment steps in the endorsement are performed by the Trust Administrator (c014, c019); the division of roles between the two is left to inference. That allocation could matter to who may present a claim or sue.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Payment is to be wired to an account \"established pursuant to the Pooling and Servicing Agreement\", with an alternative if no such account has been established that the clause does not clearly specify. The fallback leaves the payee uncertain in exactly the circumstance the proviso contemplates.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Payment of a preference claim is conditioned on delivery of a certified copy of a court order \"to the effect that the Holder is required to return principal or interest\" plus a duly executed assignment \"in such form as is reasonably required by Financial Security\"; whether these are strict conditions precedent and what form is \"reasonably required\" are both open. The assignment is described as covering \"all rights and claims of the Holder relating to or arising under the Insured Certificates\", a scope broader than its stated preference purpose.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
     {"issue": "The all-encompassing assignment demanded here is wider than the subrogation the Policy itself grants, which reaches only the Holder's \"rights ... to receive distributions\" (c004). The two transfer mechanisms describe different bundles of rights for the same payment.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.14},
     {"issue": "The obligation to cancel, reissue and deliver the Insured Certificate to Financial Security assumes physical certificates, whereas \"Holder\" is defined by reference to registration books or bearer form (c005). Whether delivery is a condition of payment or a follow-on step is not fixed by either provision.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The Trust Administrator purports to assign, \"on its behalf or on behalf of the Trustee and the Holders\", rights in respect of the Insured Certificates, without stating the authority for binding Holders or the precise content of the rights assigned. What passes to Financial Security under this assignment is the central question for any recovery action it brings.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
     {"issue": "This assignment overlaps and does not match the Policy's own subrogation clause (c004), which is limited to the Holder's right to receive distributions, and it makes the Trust Administrator rather than the Trustee named in c001/c015 the assigning party. Harmonising the two transfer provisions and the two entities is a genuine whole-instrument problem.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The further-assurances duty is measured by what is \"reasonably requested or required by Financial Security\", an undefined standard set by the party that benefits from it. Its outer limit — what a Trust Administrator can be compelled to do — is not bounded by the clause.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]}
]}

